any representation made by Purchaser in this Agreement shall have been materially false or misleading when made;
Purchaser shall have defaulted in its performance under any material provision of this Agreement; or
any proceeding is instituted against Purchaser seeking to adjudicate Purchaser as a bankrupt or insolvent, or Purchaser makes a general assignment for the benefit of its creditors, or a receiver is appointed on account of the insolvency of Purchaser, or Purchaser files a petition seeking to take advantage of any other law relating to bankruptcy, insolvency, winding up or composition or readjustment of debts and in the case of any such proceeding instituted against Purchaser (but not by Purchaser) such proceeding is not dismissed within sixty (60) days of such filing.
Seller Remedies.  The provisions of Article 26 hereof notwithstanding, if an Event of Purchaser Default shall have occurred and be continuing, Seller shall have the right to terminate this Agreement by delivery of a notice of termination to Purchaser, in addition to any rights and remedies that may be available at law or in equity.


FORCE MAJEURE
Failure to Perform Due to an Event of Force Majeure.  Subject to the terms of this Article 18, either party shall be excused from performance and shall not be considered to be in default with respect to any obligation hereunder, to the extent such party’s (the “Affected Party”) failure of performance is due to an event of force majeure as defined in this Article (the “Event of Force Majeure”).

Events of Force Majeure., the following occurrences constitute Events of Force Majeure, unless excepted  in Section 18.3 below:

explosions, fires, nuclear radiation contamination, hurricanes, earthquakes, floods, natural disasters, epidemics, other acts of God, and any other similar circumstances;
war and other hostilities (whether declared or not), revolution, public disorders, insurrection, rebellion, sabotage, acts of public officials or terrorist action;
any action or relative material inaction taken by any national or local government or judicial authority after the date of this Agreement, including without limitation any order, legislation, enactment, judgment, ruling or decision; or
national or regional strikes (to the extent affecting the Seller’s performance of Scope of Work) and strikes specific to the Site or to Seller’s and its approved Vendor’s (as listed in Exhibit B-4) manufacturing facilities.
 Notwithstanding the foregoing, the occurrences set forth in (a) through (d) above shall not be considered Events of Force Majeure if:
 (e) such circumstance is within the reasonable control of the party affected;
 (f) such circumstance, with the exercise of reasonable diligence, can be prevented, avoided or removed by such party;
 (g) such circumstance does not prevent the Affected Party from fulfilling its obligations under the Agreement;
 (h) the Affected Party has not taken all reasonable precautions, due care and reasonable alternative measures in order to avoid the effect of such event on the affected party’s ability to fulfill its obligations under the Agreement and to mitigate the consequences thereof; and
 (i) such event is the result of any failure of such party to perform any of its obligations under the Agreement.

Certain Events Not Excused.  Notwithstanding that an Event of Force Majeure may otherwise exist, the provisions of this Article 18 shall not excuse:

late delivery of equipment or materials caused by Seller, or caused by any of the subcontractors of Seller, if Seller could have avoided such late delivery by exercising all reasonable endeavors as a prudent equipment supplier;
late performance by Seller caused by (i) Seller’s failure to engage qualified subcontractors and suppliers, (ii) Seller’s failure to hire an adequate number of personnel or labor or (iii) by inefficiencies on the part of Seller; or
delays resulting from reasonably foreseeable unfavorable weather or reasonably foreseeable unsuitable ground conditions.
Notice of Event of Force Majeure.  
 (a) Promptly following the occurrence of any Event of Force Majeure, but in no event more than three (3) days after learning of such Event of Force Majeure, the party declaring that an Event of Force Majeure (i) excuses or delays the performance of any obligation hereunder or (ii) requires a potential adjustment of the Purchase Amount, shall promptly provide written notice to the other party in accordance with Section 25.1 hereof.  The Affected Party has the burden of proof to establish that an Event of Force Majeure has occurred and adversely affects its ability to perform. The Affected Party shall provide the other party, its employees or its agents or contractors, with access to its premises and equipment as soon as practicable after the occurrence of an Event of Force Majeure.
 (b) Within seven (7) days of providing notice regarding the occurrence of an Event of Force Majeure, the Affected Party shall provide a written description of (i) the Event of Force Majeure (including the nature and expected duration of such Event of Force Majeure) and (ii) measures the Affected Party has taken to avoid the effect of such Event of Force Majeure on such party’s ability to fulfill its obligations under the Agreement and to mitigate the consequences thereof.  The Affected Party shall provide any additional information concerning the Event of Force Majeure reasonably requested by the other party (including, without limitation, updating of any information already provided under this Section 18.4).
 (c) As soon as practicable following the termination of an Event of Force Majeure, the Affected Party shall submit to the other party sufficient evidence regarding the nature and extent of the delay and its effect upon (i) the Guaranteed Delivery Date or (ii) the Purchase Amount, as appropriate.
 (d) Within ten (10) days after the termination of an Event of Force Majeure the parties hereto shall meet to discuss appropriate measures necessary that should be taken, including whether extension of the Guaranteed Delivery Date(s) described in Section 10.2.1 or the Installation Period(s), or, if applicable, an adjustment in the Purchase Amount described in Section 5.1.1, by the parties to take into account the effect of such Event of Force Majeure on the ability of Purchaser and Seller to reschedule project activities to avoid or minimize overall delays or additional costs resulting from the Event of Force Majeure. 
 (g) The parties  shall (i) make all reasonable efforts to prevent, reduce to a minimum and mitigate the effect of any delay or potential adjustment of the Purchase Amount occasioned by any Event of Force Majeure, including recourse to alternate acceptable source of services, equipment and materials and construction equipment; and (ii) shall use their best efforts to ensure resumption of normal performance of this Agreement after the occurrence of any Event of Force Majeure and shall perform their obligations as agreed between the parties to the maximum extent practicable.

Continued Performance.  Upon the occurrence of any Event of Force Majeure, the parties shall endeavor to continue to perform their obligations under the Agreement so far as reasonably practicable and Seller shall during the period of such circumstances protect and secure the works in such manner as Purchaser shall require.  Seller shall notify Purchaser of the steps he proposes to take including any reasonable alternative means for performance of the works not prevented by the Event of Force Majeure.

Event of Force Majeure - Delays.  If either party becomes unable to perform all or part of its obligations under this Agreement because of an Event of Force Majeure, and the Affected Party has properly invoked and observed the provisions of Section 18.4 in respect thereof, the Affected Party shall be permitted a delay in the performance of its obligations affected by the Event of Force Majeure and an extension of the Guaranteed Delivery Date or the Installation Period as applicable.

Event of Force Majeure - Cost.  Seller shall bear its own delay costs occasioned by any Event of Force Majeure for the first thirty (30) Day period during the occurrence or continuance of each such Event of Force Majeure.  If an Event of Force Majeure continues beyond such thirty (30) Day period in which Purchaser is the Affected Party, Seller shall be entitled, subject to the provisions of Section 11.3, to recover costs occasioned by each such Event of Force Majeure which accrue after each such thirty (30) Day period pursuant to a Purchase Amount adjustment in accordance with Section 5.3 and Article 11 hereof.

Cancellation for Force Majeure.  Notwithstanding that Seller may have been granted under Section 10.2.4 an extension of a Guaranteed Delivery Date(s), if by virtue of Section 18.1 either party shall be excused the performance of any obligation for a continuous period of one hundred eighty (180) days, then Purchaser may at any time thereafter, and provided such performance is still excused, terminate this Agreement by notice to Seller.

Payment on Cancellation for Force Majeure.  If the Agreement is canceled under Section 18.8, Seller shall be entitled to be paid pursuant to Sections 5.4.1 and 5.4.2, plus the amount of any other expenditure which in the circumstances was reasonably incurred by Seller in the expectation of completing the whole of the Scope of Work; but Seller shall not be entitled to any other payment, including, without limitation, any payment in respect of anticipated profit on this Agreement.


